We still only have room to grow.

470
00:37:32,056 --> 00:37:34,556
悪者扱いして来た街で
In the town where I was treated like a villain,

471
00:37:35,056 --> 00:37:37,056
悪者扱いして来たオトナへ
to the adult who was treated like a villain,

472
00:37:37,556 --> 00:37:40,056
変わりゆく俺、鏡の中へ
I change, into the mirror,

473
00:37:40,556 --> 00:37:42,556
尋ねても答えなら yeah yeah yeah
even if I ask, there's no answer, yeah yeah yeah.

474
00:37:43,056 --> 00:37:45,556
去る者追わない引くところ引いて
Don't chase those who leave, pull where you pull,

475
00:37:46,056 --> 00:37:48,056
丸く納めたり軽くいなして
round it up and lightly vanish,

476
00:37:48,856 --> 00:37:51,056
鏡の中で嗤ってるお前
you who are laughing in the mirror,

477
00:37:51,356 --> 00:37:53,556
括れやしなかったわ。たったの三文字で
weren't you bracing yourself? Just three words.

478
00:37:54,356 --> 00:37:56,556
日日重くなる足取りで
With heavy footsteps day by day,

479
00:37:57,056 --> 00:37:59,056
自分の歩幅で闊歩してる
I'm walking at my own pace.

480
00:37:59,056 --> 00:38:01,556
勘ぐるとこ勘ぐり
Guess where, leave where,

481
00:38:01,556 --> 00:38:04,056
割と適当な段取りで
with a fairly casual pacing,

482
00:38:04,556 --> 00:38:07,056
やっと思い付いて来たかも
maybe I've finally started to understand

483
00:38:07,256 --> 00:38:09,856
このポンコツの操縦の仕方を
how to handle this ponkotsu.

484
00:38:10,056 --> 00:38:13,556
19の時の「ついに来たか...」よりももっと清々しい気持ち
With a much fresher feeling than "Finally came..." at 19,

485
00:38:17,056 --> 00:38:19,556
隅田川にかかる勝鬨橋を渡る
Crossing Kachidoki Bridge over the Sumida River,

486
00:38:22,056 --> 00:38:24,556
左手にスカイツリー 右手に東京タワー
Skytree on the left, Tokyo Tower on the right,

487
00:38:27,556 --> 00:38:29,556
俺はその真ん中
I am right in the middle.

488
00:38:29,950 --> 00:38:32,056
サボり方とか甘え方とか
Laziness or spoiling,

489
00:38:32,056 --> 00:38:34,556
逃げ方とか言い訳の仕方とか
running away or making excuses,

490
00:38:34,856 --> 00:38:37,056
やっと覚えてきた身につけてきた
I've finally learned and picked them up.

491
00:38:37,556 --> 00:38:39,856
柔らかい頭
Soft head,

492
00:38:40,056 --> 00:38:42,556
カッコの付け方調子のこき方
how to wear a cap, how things are going,

493
00:38:43,056 --> 00:38:45,556
腹の据え方良い年のこき方
how to hold one's ground, how to have a good year,

494
00:38:45,856 --> 00:38:48,556
脂乗りに乗った濁った目した
riding the gravy train, having a cloudy look,

495
00:38:48,856 --> 00:38:51,056
だらしない身体
sloppy body.

496
00:38:52,056 --> 00:38:55,056
幸せの体感速度は早くなるばかり
The speed of feeling happy only gets faster,

497
00:38:56,556 --> 00:39:00,056
傷が癒えていく速度は遅くなるばかり
the speed at which wounds heal only gets slower,

498
00:39:02,056 --> 00:39:06,056
他人には期待をしないのが今の俺の強み
not expecting anything from others is my strength now,

499
00:39:07,056 --> 00:39:11,556
手荷物でも進める距離なら行くぜ欺き欺き
even with a heavy load, if the distance is manageable, I'll go, deceiving myself.

500
00:39:12,056 --> 00:39:16,556
身の程を知る程に胸を張りいつもの通り
Knowing my own limits, I always puff out my chest,

501
00:39:16,856 --> 00:39:21,056
でも時にしたって良い背伸び
but sometimes a good stretch of the back is in order,

502
00:39:19,856 --> 00:39:24,056
やっと「大人げない」が出来る年
a year where I can finally act "un-adult-like."

503
00:39:23,456 --> 00:39:27,556
小さな枠組みただの数字
Small framework, just a number,

504
00:39:26,356 --> 00:39:29,856
縛られずにでも腹くくり
unbound, yet with a firm belly,

505
00:39:29,456 --> 00:39:33,556
あの日の俺が立ち止まる程にデカくそびえ立つ
so big and towering that the me of that day stops in its tracks.

506
00:39:34,456 --> 00:39:39,056
隅田川にかかる勝鬨橋を渡る
Crossing Kachidoki Bridge over the Sumida River,

507
00:39:40,456 --> 00:39:45,056
重なるスカイツリー 東京タワーと真ん中の頼りない背中
heavy Skytree, right in the middle of Tokyo Tower, with an unreliable back.

508
00:39:46,657 --> 00:39:50,056
サボり方とか甘え方とか
Laziness or spoiling,

509
00:39:49,056 --> 00:39:52,556
逃げ方とか言い訳の仕方とか
running away or making excuses,

510
00:39:51,856 --> 00:39:55,056
やっと覚えてきた身につけてきた
I've finally learned and picked them up.

511
00:39:54,756 --> 00:39:58,056
柔らかい頭
Soft head,

512
00:40:00,104 --> 00:40:03,424
春の風に吹かれて 綿毛 ふわり 横切っていく
Blowin' in the spring breeze, fluffy dandelion fluff drifts across.

513
00:40:03,624 --> 00:40:06,924
どこまで行くのかな 僕もたどり着けるかな
I wonder how far it goes, and if I'll reach there too.

514
00:40:07,124 --> 00:40:10,424
ふっと歩みを止めて 振り返って見る自分は
